WEBVTT

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.900
You're living with a minor?

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.670
Yeah. I knew them when we were little, 
and they ran away from home.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.080
Since when?

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.040
A few months ago.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.320
So, um, just so we're clear.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.030
Is it a girl? A boy?

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.760
Do I really have to say?

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:35.560
Yoshida-kun, I'm sure you know this, 
but that's very close to a crime.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:41.300
And can you swear 
you won't fall in love with her?

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.230
I can!

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.220
I see.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:48.070
If you're that insistent, 
then let me see her.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.690
Hello, Sayu-chan!

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:57.800
I'm Gotou.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.500
For starters...

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.080
Why don't we have some snacks?

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:45.430
So basically you grabbed some girl off the street 
and let her stay with you?

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.600
"Reality"

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:49.630
I was suspicious when you started talking about 
how you knew her when you were young,

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.120
even though I didn't ask.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.660
You're surprisingly bold, Yoshida-kun.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:01.180
Sayu-chan, did he do anything weird to you?

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.170
Gotou-san!

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.420
Nothing.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:08.200
I'm honestly surprised.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.390
"Surprised," huh?

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.480
Well, it seems he's not into younger girls.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:18.740
You got lucky.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:24.110
Even if I were, I wouldn't do anything.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.340
I don't know about that.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:31.270
Hey! I'm not that kind of guy!

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:33.440
I'm joking!

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.070
What's wrong?

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.530
No. It's nothing.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.740
It didn't look like "nothing" to me.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.400
It's nothing, really.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.700
I just may have had a bit too much for dinner.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.030
I see.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:00.600
I'm gonna use the bathroom.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.270
Okay.

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.340
Hey, Sayu-chan.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:12.860
Yes?

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.600
I'd like to talk to you in private.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.800
Private?

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.400
Yes.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.380
You have something you want to ask me, too?

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.370
So how about it?

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:35.960
Thank you!

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.700
Um, Yoshida-san. 
Sorry... but I have a request.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.320
Eggs, chives, and miso right?

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:57.500
You're really okay alone with her?

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.540
Yeah. I'm fine.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.540
I see.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:03.950
Okay, off I go.

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:05.320
Bye!

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.920
He's gone.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.050
Thanks.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.270
No...

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.380
Can I go first?

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:36.350
Okay.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.850
Is it true you're in high school?

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:41.590
It is.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.920
Where did you come from?

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.420
Hokkaido.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.580
When did you leave home?

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:51.000
About six months ago.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.450
Why?

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:57.160
I don't want to answer that.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:01.130
All right. I understand.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:06.260
I won't ask you about 
how you got here or why you left.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:12.260
But there's something 
I need to make absolutely clear.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:16.620
As Yoshida-kun's friend.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:21.270
And this is something that only
I, a complete stranger, can ask.

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:25.440
How long are you going to stay here?

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:29.860
What are you doing here?

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.520
I went to the movie theater at the station.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.410
But this is the opposite way 
from the station.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.500
I felt like taking a walk.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:44.270
What about you, Yoshida-senpai?

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:48.600
I got asked to buy some stuff for breakfast.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.190
By who?

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.050
Who else but Sayu?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.930
Is she at your place now?

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.910
Yes, of course she is.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:01.350
She doesn't have anywhere else to go.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:04.410
I see.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.490
Senpai, can I go shopping with you?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.480
No answer, huh?

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:34.550
Teenage kids are special.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.900
No matter how much you struggle,

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:42.340
right now you can't be anything 
but a high-school girl.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:46.190
That's how powerful that label is.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:52.440
No matter what you do, 
you'll never be anything but a high-school girl.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:56.810
Whether you intend to use that label 
for your own benefit or not...

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.900
Yoshida-kun might be fine with it, 
but society won't be.

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:13.840
Thank you.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:20.680
I told myself that I wanted to
run away from everything—to just forget.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:27.150
But I think what I actually wanted 
was for somebody to tell me not to run away.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:33.590
I've stayed with a lot of men 
since I left home.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.870
Um...

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:39.860
Letting them use my body...

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:45.290
Something inside me just went crazy.

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:49.640
I let them use me just to have a place 
to stay for a few nights.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:55.860
And sometimes, when they wanted me, 
it made me feel good.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:04.060
But Yoshida-san told me that 
what I was doing wasn't right.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.220
Not only did he not do anything to me,

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.070
he told me he'd set me straight.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:17.820
Sorry...

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:20.980
I know this is serious, but...

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.080
I can just see it in my head.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:32.300
I'm glad you found a place 
where you can be safe.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:38.050
Yeah...

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:45.270
Yoshida-kun accepts you. And you trust him.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:49.100
I can tell that easily by watching you.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.870
So it's okay for you 
to let him be nice to you.

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:57.590
I'm sure of that.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:09:59.620
But...

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:06.070
That's okay only if it's done 
in the right way.

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:08.060
You know what I mean, right?

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:15.470
I do.

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:18.740
So you can take your time with it, but think.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.640
About what you'll do next.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:29.820
My past and where I was were things 
I just had to get away from.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:32.410
No, that's still true.

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:33.210
Yeah.

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:39.580
Just thinking about it 
makes me want to throw up.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:42.140
And I don't want to go back at all.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:47.430
But I know I can't keep doing this forever.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:51.540
So I'll face my past,

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:55.260
leave here, and go back to where I was.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:01.770
For my sake, and Yoshida-san's sake.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.520
Good.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.320
As long you feel that way, you'll be okay.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:20.650
You get to be a high-school girl 
for only a short part of your life.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.510
So face the things you need to face.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:26.190
Accept the kindness you need to accept.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:28.600
Live your life.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:33.430
Whether you go to high school or not, 
you're a high-schooler.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.630
Take care on your way home.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.750
I want to ask you something.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:11.870
If I asked to stay at your place tonight, 
would you let me?

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:14.390
What does that mean?

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:17.260
It means just what I said.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:21.900
Why do I have to let someone stay over 
if she's not my girlfriend?

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:24.760
Sayu-chan's not your girlfriend, right?

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:27.900
I'm just looking after her.

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:30.310
What about Gotou-san?

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.250
What about Gotou-san?

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:39.900
Why are you talking about her?

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:42.490
And why won't you answer my question?

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.360
What are you talking about?

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:47.160
She's at your place right now, isn't she?

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:50.700
How did you know?

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:58.830
The two of you were whispering to each other, 
and it was suspicious, so I got curious.

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:03.930
You were acting weird 
when you left the yakiniku place.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:09.530
And then, she got off 
at your station with you!

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:15.690
So I got off as well, 
and just kind of followed you.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:18.620
And you were heading to the residential area,

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:22.520
so I realized you were both going 
to your place.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:31.390
Um... I'm sorry for being a stalker.

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:33.070
I apologize for that.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.340
No, it's not really...

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:41.080
But Yoshida-san, whenever I ask about her, 
you won't give me a straight answer.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:46.540
It makes me sad, 
as if you're hiding something from me.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:48.590
Hey...

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:49.890
I'm sorry.

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:01.860
So, didn't you have a question for me?

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.190
Gotou-san...

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:12.780
Are you in love with Yoshida-san?

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:22.270
Wait, was that what you wanted to ask? 
Is that it?

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:23.780
It's important.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:26.090
To who?

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:30.250
To me.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:32.630
And to Yoshida-san, too!

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:40.760
He loves you.

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:42.190
Does that bother you?

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.170
That's not the issue here!

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:49.190
Don't get mad. You're so cute, really.

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:53.530
I do.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.910
I'm not interested in anybody else.

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:58.250
Really?

00:14:59.010 --> 00:15:01.870
Why would I lie?

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:06.540
Because it's hard to know 
what you're really thinking.

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:08.680
I like being a mysterious woman.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:11.290
It makes you hard to deal with.

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:13.970
You came out and said it, huh?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.850
I really do like him.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:23.800
I've been watching him 
since he came to the company.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.150
Good.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:28.830
"Good"?

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:33.550
I'm really happy he'll get the girl he loves.

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:36.100
Will you support me?

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:39.620
O-Of course I will!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:40.860
Thank you!

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:54.840
I thought you'd taken Gotou-san home 
to sleep with you, since Sayu-chan was gone.

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:59.610
Why wouldn't Sayu be at home, though?

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.480
I don't get it.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:09.480
Let me ask you this. 
You still like Gotou-san, right?

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:14.080
Yeah. I couldn't give up on her 
that quickly.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.990
Then what you're doing doesn't make sense.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:18.940
How?

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:21.670
The girl you love is coming to your house!

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:28.230
And you're letting some random teenager 
be in the same room. It's weird.

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:31.530
Well, I'll admit it's weird.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.840
But there's nothing I can do about it.

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:39.600
Why? The woman you've always loved, 
and some random teenager.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:41.670
You can't even compare the two.

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:47.800
Listen. Is what you're trying to say here 
that I should kick out Sayu?

00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:51.670
No. That's not it.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:57.870
I'm asking about what your priority is.

00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:00.830
Priority?

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.330
That's right.

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:07.720
If I were you, and I really
wanted to date Gotou-san,

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:09.690
I'd hide Sayu-chan.

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:15.390
But if I did that and ended up dating Gotou-san, 
I'd have to kick her out!

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:16.630
And that's why—

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.830
I'm sorry!

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:23.360
No.

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:28.730
I know that you're not the kind
of person who can do that.

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:32.440
But at the same time I wonder...

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:36.540
That's not really love, is it?

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:40.780
I mean your feelings toward Gotou-san.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:44.100
It's a mix of actual love 
and simple admiration.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:45.980
No, it's not.

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:52.130
Or maybe your feelings toward
Sayu-chan are changing?

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:54.600
I can tell you that isn't true!

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:56.110
It's not?

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:58.680
Then you're just too nice.

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:07.420
And when you're too nice,
you won't get the things you really want.

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:15.740
Sorry.

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:19.980
If I stay here any longer, 
I'm likely to say something else I shouldn't.

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:21.870
So I'm going to go home.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.280
Okay...

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:25.820
Okay, bye!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:33.920
Bye!

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.390
I'm back.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.600
What are you doing?

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:53.750
Can't you tell? Makeup!

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:56.360
And we're done!

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.250
Welcome back.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:01.720
Yoshida-san, what do you think?

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:07.250
W-Well... I guess it looks good.

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.920
There's nothing else you can say?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:15.800
That's right. If you can't compliment a girl 
when she changes something,

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.160
no girls will like you!

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:18.470
That's right!

00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:31.420
She's a good girl, huh?

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:32.530
Huh?

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:34.500
I mean Sayu-chan.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.040
She's a great girl.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:39.500
Well, yeah. She is.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:41.740
And that's why you couldn't just leave her?

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:45.420
No, I don't know about that.

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:49.200
Well, I think that's okay.

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:50.560
Huh?

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:52.460
Nothing!

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:56.460
Don't try anything with her.

00:19:56.460 --> 00:20:00.840
The two of us have a hotline now.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.810
I won't!

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.180
And...

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:14.650
Watch over her.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:17.020
Of course. That's the plan.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:20.860
I wouldn't let a teenage girl stay at my place 
if I weren't serious about taking care of her.

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:28.950
But she's unstable 
and doesn't understand herself at all.

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:40.310
So there's no telling what feelings she has 
that might suddenly burst out.

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:45.560
Well, you'll be okay no matter what happens.

00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:47.450
What?

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:48.910
Don't you know?

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:54.730
The bosses at work all call you 
the problem-solver.

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:04.160
You always go out of your way 
to get involved with the biggest problems.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:06.410
Give me a break.

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:09.660
I'm cheering for you.

00:21:10.340 --> 00:21:14.460
With work, and Sayu-chan, too!

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:19.590
Thanks.

00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:57.810
What? You didn't hear?

00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:02.400
That new girl that started here. 
Sayu-chaso! Sayu-chaso!

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:06.300
I think I did see her name on the shift list.

00:23:06.300 --> 00:23:08.490
She's a high-school girl, right?

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:12.280
Yeah. And super-duper cute, too!

00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:14.310
Super-duper cute?

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:16.680
I'll look forward to that.

00:23:17.920 --> 00:23:21.540
I'll rip your head off if you
lay a hand on her.

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:35.010
"Starry Sky"

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Girls won't like you 
if you don't watch next week!</b>
